cred song-book, a collection of songs in praise of the heroes of Israel, a “book of golden deeds,” a national anthology.","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[18]}],"places":[{"id":"ziklag_1259","name":"Ziklag","kind":"City","lat":31.38256,"lon":34.86676,"summary":"A town in the Negeb, or south country of Judah (Josh. 15:31), in the possession of the Philistines when David fled to Gath from Ziph with all his followers.","verses":12,"v":[1]},{"id":"mount_gilboa_837","name":"mount Gilboa","kind":"Mountain","lat":32.50984,"lon":35.40843,"summary":"","verses":5,"v":[6]},{"id":"ashkelon_103","name":"Ashkelon","kind":"City","lat":31.66426,"lon":34.54732,"summary":"Askelon=Ascalon, was one of the five cities of the Philistines (Josh. 13:3; 1 Sam. 6:17). It stood on the shore of the Mediterranean, 12 miles north of Gaza.","verses":11,"v":[20]},{"id":"gath_442","name":"Gath","kind":"City","lat":31.69353,"lon":34.84388,"summary":"A wine-vat, one of the five royal cities of the Philistines (Josh. 13:3) on which the ark brought calamity (1 Sam. 5:8, 9; 6:17). It was famous also as being the birthplace or residence of Goliath (1 Sam. 17:4).","verses":32,"v":[20]},{"id":"gilboa_474","name":"Gilboa","kind":"Region","lat":32.51667,"lon":35.4,"summary":"Boiling spring, a mountain range, now Jebel Fukua’, memorable as the scene of Saul’s disastrous defeat by the Philistines. Here also his three sons were slain, and he himself died by his own hand (1 Sam. 28:4; 31:1-8; 2 Sam. 1:6-21; 21:12; 1 Chr. 10:1, 8).","verses":3,"v":[21]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[310,4194,4194,7586,7586,1732,7725,5221,5221,5221,853,6002,6002,3427,3427,6860,6860,8147,3117],[7992,7992,7992,3117,376,376,7167,7167,899,127,127,5921,7218,7218,935,4480,7586,4264,935,935,935,413,1732,5307,5307,776,776,776,7812,7812,7812,7812],[335,935,935,935,935,1732,559,4422,4422,4422,3478,3478,3478,4264,559,559],[4100,1961,1961,1961,1732,559,4994,5046,0,5971,5971,5127,4480,442